{"kind":"assert","text":"The blocker this request names has half landed, and the half that has not needs an actor with ratifier authority. Measured against the log at sequence 3151.\n\nThe guidance landed. AGENTS.md now forbids recording a merge artifact at path dot, and no live artifact at that path has been recorded since sequence 2420 — roughly seven hundred events ago — so merges are following it.\n\nThe migration did not. 55 artifacts are still live at path dot, against 38 retired there. That is the condition this request says makes the structural succession rule unsound, and it is unchanged: while a live dot artifact exists, every retired dot artifact is rescued by it, which is the over-broad rescue rather than genuine succession.\n\nRecomputing the numbers this request states, against the log as it stands today: of 204 retired artifacts, 182 have a later live artifact at the same exact path and 22 do not. The 22 condemned matches the count measured when the request was written, and none of them sit at path dot — still the symptom it identified rather than evidence of health.\n\nTwo things block the migration, and neither is implementation. First, authority: AGENTS.md is explicit that the fold admits a supersession only from the artifact author or from an actor holding ratifier, that more than one actor recorded these artifacts, and that hugh is therefore the only actor who can retire the whole set. I am a bare participant and can retire only my own; running it as anyone else would produce a run of ineffective supersessions. Second, the quiet-wave gate: AGENTS.md says to wait until no review request is still awaiting its first verdict. That count is 19 right now, so the gate is not open, and most of those 19 are review requests waiting on codex.\n\nSo this request cannot proceed yet, and not for want of someone to do the work. It needs the review queue to drain and then hugh to run the retirement. Recording the measurement so the next reader does not re-derive it, and so the dependency is visible as a number rather than as a sentence.\n\nOne caveat on the gate: the same query reports 51 of 94 named artifact references not resolving to a live artifact. AGENTS.md says a non-zero value there is worth looking at before trusting the awaiting count. I have not investigated those 51. A large share are probably requests whose artifacts were legitimately retired at merge, but I have not proved that and am not claiming it."}